 {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe common activities at work to a visitor using short sentences in familiar spoken and written situations.  Give detailed information related to UML and common related topics.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations.  Describes common activities related to Software Programming through the use of appropriate expressions, grammar and vocabulary in written or spoken situations according to the abilities related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}]}, {"content": "enpe7n4le02ob08re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "run-time ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " that happens during the execution of a program", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They're very useful when you've got to control run-time instances that collaborate by using communication links.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le02ob08aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "cooperation ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the act of working together towards a common goal", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This kind of diagram works by enabling collaboration, which shows cooperation between different instances\u2026", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le02ob08aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "accomplish ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to finish something successfully", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: CS diagrams can show boxes containing a classifier which shows steps to follow to accomplish something. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le02ob08aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "enroll ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to enlist, to register ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: For example, the different stages to enroll in a course, such as the requirements, selection tests, form completion, etc.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le02ob08aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "notation ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "system of symbols that you use in specific fields", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You're right Sally! But you haven't got to confuse them, it's important to note that this similarity mostly relates to their notation. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le02ob08aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "guidance ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "advice or counseling teachers or tutors provide to students", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: I guess I'll ask you for more guidance before I start using this diagram.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le02ob08aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Look for information about a process where you study. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Check the parts and roles involved in the process", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write at least 3 parts and 3 roles.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Draw your own boxes and describe how they will collaborate and the steps to achieve the goal.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your drawing with you classmates. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I look for information about a process.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I draw a diagram related to a process. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my findings with my partners. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Future Time Clauses (Before and After)", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the <b>future tense</b> to talk about the distant future or events that you have not planned.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Future time clauses are dependent clauses that you can link to an independent clause; the <span class=\"italic\">independent clause </span>is the one you write using <span class=\"italic\">future simple, </span>and you connect it to the independent clause using <span class=\"italic\">before </span>and <span class=\"italic\">after</span>. </br></br>  You can use a simple present sentence or you can use a verb in <span class=\"italic\">-ing form </span>after <i>before</i> and <i>after</i>. </br></br>  Examples:</br> <span class=\"italic\"> I'll start using that diagram <strong>after</strong> we reach an agreement. </br> I'll start using that diagram <strong>after </strong>reaching an agreement. </br> We won't discard the design <strong>before </strong>we finish the project. </br> We won't discard the design <strong>before</strong> finishing the project. </br></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Before we start talking about it, I will tell you that you haven't got to keep your questions to yourselves, you can ask any questions if you need to. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "No. I guess I'll ask you for more guidance before I start using this diagram.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Have Got (Negative Sentences) ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <b>have got</b> to talk about obligations and needs.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "In order to use <strong>have got</strong>, you need to take into account that the verb <i>have</i> changes depending on the subject it follows: </br>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b><center>Pronoun\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b><center>Have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>I\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>You\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>He\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>has\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>She\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>has\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>It\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>has\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>We\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>They\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"have\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": " You can use <b>have got</b> in negative sentences to show that there is no obligation to do something, or also to show that you don't have possession of a noun. </br></br>  Examples: </br><span class=\"italic\">  I <strong>haven't got</strong> to use this type of diagram because I have got to use the composite structure diagram. </br> She <strong>hasn't got</strong> to know all the types of diagrams. </br> He <strong>hasn't got</strong> any computers to work with.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You're right Sally! But you haven't got to confuse them.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Before we start talking about it, I will tell you that you haven't got to keep your questions to yourselves, you can ask any questions if you need to.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "List of Programming and Computer Science Terms", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "There are many <b>terms</b> that computer science has adopted to refer to the different activities or processes that surround it. You need to know them to be able to communicate with your colleagues and even understand manuals or instructions.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Editor\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"An editor can be a computer program that allows you to edit or modify a file. It can also refer to the person who makes those modifications.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Emacs\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It refers to a group of text editors that contain over 2000 commands which is commonly used in macros to make work automatic.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Emulation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It is when a system simulates the conditions and behaviors of another one. It also includes the use of virtual machines.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Emulator\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A piece of hardware or software that imitates or simulates the behaviors of another one. In this case, the system that wants to imitate the other is called the host, and the one that is simulated is called the guest.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Entropy\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A condition of randomness in computing that allows for data to be encoded. It is a key component in security and performance.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}]}